================================================================================
THREAD F SYNTHESIS (mac-mini-2026-06-20-SF) — the precise S3-closing statement
================================================================================

THE EXACT SUFFICIENT CONDITION (chain, with status):
  THM-523/525/526: LRC(14)-S3 <= every primitive covering 13-set S=P∪L (k=|L|>=3,
    k<=2 proved) has M(S)>=1/14.   [PROVED reduction]
  THM-532/HYP-2603: N(E) ⊆ S7(E)  (a 1/7-net hits every sector), so
    meas(S7(E)) <= cap_k := min_{|P|=13-k} meas(G_P)  ⟹  μ_{1/7}>=thr_k ⟹ S3.
    [PROVED set-inclusion; the THM-527-A finite-Vmax glue is the upstream caveat]
  THM-534: meas(S7(E)) = p0(E) = q_E(R={1..6}) is the SINGLE LRC predicate.
    [PROVED: p0 = full-cover residual capacity, |R|=6 layer of the cone]

  ==> S3-CLOSING CONDITION (exact, canonical):
        for all primitive E (0∈E, |E|=k, k=8..12):  p0(E) = meas(S7(E)) <= cap_k.
      The cone Σ_R w_R q_C(R) (HYP-2697/2698) is a PROOF DEVICE for this, NOT a
      stronger/alternative predicate. The LRC predicate reads ONLY R={1..6}.

cap_k = min_{|P|=13-k} meas(G_P):  2243/5880, 1979/4004, 55/91, 66/91, 6/7 (k=8..12).
  cap_k >= (k-6)/7 PROVED (subadditivity, THM-535-A). k=8 anomalous: P*={1,5,7,8,9}.

WIDE(A)+FINITE(B) PARTITION (do they close p0<=cap?):
  FINITE (Thread B, span<=N): exhaustive box exact, consec maximizes p0,
    p0<=cap, 0 violators k=8,9,10 (verified above, box<=13). THM-536-B2 span-floor
    N*=7,8,10,13,20,20 (k=8..13); THM-535 closes k>=9 via (k-6)/7. Need W(k) explicit
    & box>=N*: box B18/B17 already covers k=8,9 to span 18, k=10..12 to 17. FEASIBLE.
  WIDE (Thread A, span>W): iid_k=7!S(k,7)/7^k = 0.0245/0.0577/0.1049/0.1631/0.2285;
    cap_k - iid_k = 0.357/0.437/0.499/0.562/0.629 (LARGE budget). High relation-height
    ⟹ corr small ⟹ p0≈iid≪cap. VERIFIED, the BV/Erdos-Turan decorrelation bound NOT
    yet a closed inequality (THM-546/HYP-2684).

ANSWER TO "does the cone need more than p0<=cap?":  NO for the predicate.
  The cone's small-|R| violations (HYP-2700a, e.g. K=consec_8 vs C=(0..6,8):
  q_C(R=(1,3,5))=223/420 > q_K=129/245; q_C(R=(1,))>q_K) are INTERNAL to a
  cone-based PROOF of consec-max-p0; they do NOT violate p0(E)<=cap. The
  full-cover layer |R|=6 (=p0) has 0 violators k=8,9,10 (HYP-2700a).
  HYP-2700b: U4=p0+p5+5p6 OVERSHOOTS cap (U4(consec_8)=353/735>cap_8) — so the
  U4/Bonferroni4 gate (HYP-2693) is a SEPARATE, STRICTLY STRONGER true-wide gate,
  NOT the S3-closing predicate. p0<=cap is the right (weaker, sufficient) object.
